<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Oklahoma harvest in high gear.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Oklahoma harvest in high gear.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oklahoma's harvest was running in high gear Thursday, and cutting was underway in portions of south central Kansas as warm, dry weather hovered over the central U.S. Plains, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're seeing good yields, good weights, good weather,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;The only thing we need is trucks.&quot;</p>
<p>Harvesting was gearing up in Kingman and Reno counties in south central Kansas, but dealers said it was still too early to discuss yield numbers there.</p>
<p>&quot;I've heard dockage is low and test weights are in the 60s, but I don't have any numbers on yields,&quot; a dealer said.  </p>
